      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the volume of both cubes and then find the ratio of these volumes.\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the first cube (edge length of 6 inches):**\n   \\[\n   V_1 = \\text{side length}^3 = (6 \\text{ inches})^3 = 6^3 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert edge length of the second cube to inches:**\n   \\[\n   1 \\text{ foot} = 12 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n   Hence,\n   \\[\n   1 \\text{ foot} = (12 \\text{ inches})^3 = 12^3 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the ratio of the volumes:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{6^3}{12^3}\n   \\]\n\nTo solve this, we first express both volumes as powers of 2:\n      \\[\n      6^3 = (2\\cdot 3)^3 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^3\n      \\]\n      \\[\n      12^3 = (3\\cdot 4)^3 = 3^3 \\cdot 4^3\n      \\]\n   \nThen, we can find the ratio:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{2^3 \\cdot 3^3}{3^3 \\cdot 4^3} = \\frac{2^3}{4^3}\n   \\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{2^3}{(2^2)^3} = \\frac{2^3}{2^6} = \\frac{1}{2^3} = \\frac{1}{8}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches to the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot is:\n\\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\\)",
