      "text": "Let's denote the volume of the first cube as \\(V_1\\) and the volume of the second cube as \\(V_2\\). The volume of a cube is given by the formula \\(V = s^3\\), where \\(s\\) is the length of a side of the cube.\n\nGiven:\n- The edge length of the first cube is \\(s_1 = 6\\) inches.\n- The edge length of the second cube is \\(s_2 = 12\\) inches (since 1 foot = 12 inches).\n\nThe volume of the first cube is:\n\\[V_1 = s_1^3 = 6^3 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\\]\n\nThe volume of the second cube is:\n\\[V_2 = s_2^3 = 12^3 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\\]\n\nWe need to find the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube:\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{216}{1728}\\), we can divide both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor (GCD). The GCD of 216 and 1728 is 216. So:\n\\[\n\\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube is \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given side lengths in inches\ns1 = 6\ns2 = 12\n\n# Calculate volumes\nV1 = s1 ** 3\nV2 = s2 ** 3\n\n# Calculate the ratio\nratio = V1 / V2\n\n# Simplify the ratio to a common fraction\nnumerator = V1\ndenominator = V2\n\n# Find the greatest common divisor\ngcd = math.gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // gcd\nsimplified_denominator = denominator // gcd\n\nsimplified_ratio = (simplified_numerator, simplified_denominator)\nprint(simplified_ratio)\n```\n```output\n(1, 8)\n```\nThe ratio of the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches to the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\\).",
