      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the ratio of the volume of a cube with an edge length of 6 inches to the volume of a cube with an edge length of 1 foot. Let's proceed step-by-step to find the final answer.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches\nThe volume \\(V\\) of a cube with edge length \\(a\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\nV = a^3\n\\]\n\nFor a cube with edge length \\(6\\) inches:\n\\[\nV_{6 \\text{ inches}} = 6^3\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute \\(6^3\\):\n\\[\n6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot\nSince 1 foot is a longer unit than 6 inches, we convert the edge length of the large cube to inches for consistency:\n\\[\n1 \\text{ foot} = 12 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate the volume \\(V\\) of the cube with an edge length \\(12\\) inches:\n\\[\nV_{12 \\text{ inches}} = 12^3\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute \\(12^3\\):\n\\[\n12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the ratio of the two volumes\nThe ratio of the volume of the smaller cube to the volume of the larger cube is:\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_{12 \\text{ inches}}}{V_{6 \\text{ inches}}} = \\frac{1728 \\text{ cubic inches}}{216 \\text{ cubic inches}}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{1728}{216}\\), we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1728 and 216. \n\nObserving the prime factorizations:\n\\[\n1728 = 2^6 \\times 3^3\n\\]\n\\[\n216 = 2^3 \\times 3^3\n\\]\n\nThe GCD is:\n\\[\n2^3 \\times 3^3 = 8 \\times 27 = 216\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{1728}{216} = \\frac{1728 \\div 216}{216 \\div 216} = \\frac{8}{1} = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the smaller cube (6 inches) to the volume of the larger cube (1 foot) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
